Chapter: AnnotationsQuery
  cites Works chapter Annotation
  cites Works chapter AnnotationsSidecar
  cites Foreword chapter Maybe

 Asking a sidecar a question. `AnnotationsSidecar` loads the JSON and folds
 it into a store; this is the other half, the one a maintainer runs on
 purpose.

 It is deliberately a SIDE QUERY and not a build step. Not every annotation
 is worth reading, and none is worth reading every time -- a rationale
 attached to a function nobody is touching is noise on a build that would
 otherwise say nothing. So nothing here is wired to a gate, to `build.ps1`,
 or to the compiler. It answers when asked.

 It works on the flat `List Annotation` that `parse-sidecar` returns rather
 than on `AnnotationFact`. The fact's store is a HamtMap keyed by hash and
 by target, which answers "what is on this target" well and cannot be walked
 to answer "what invariants exist in this chapter" at all. The list can.

 Kinds are compared through `annotation-kind-name` rather than by matching
 the variant, so a new kind costs one line in `Annotation` and none here.

Section: Loading

 A sidecar that fails to parse answers the empty list rather than a
 diagnostic. That is the right shape for a query: the caller asked what is
 annotated, and the answer for an unreadable file is "nothing I can show
 you". A caller who needs to tell an empty sidecar from a broken one calls
 `parse-sidecar` directly and reads the Maybe.

  annq-parse : Text, Text -> List Annotation
  annq-parse (chapter) (json-text) =
    when parse-sidecar chapter json-text
      is None -> []
      is Just (xs) -> xs

Section: Filters

  annq-by-kind : List Annotation, Text -> List Annotation
  annq-by-kind (xs) (kind-name) =
    annq-by-kind-loop xs kind-name 0 (list-length xs) []

  annq-by-kind-loop : List Annotation, Text, Integer, Integer, List Annotation -> List Annotation
  annq-by-kind-loop (xs) (kind-name) (i) (len) (acc) =
    if i >= len then acc
    else annq-by-kind-step xs kind-name i len acc (list-at xs i)

  annq-by-kind-step : List Annotation, Text, Integer, Integer, List Annotation, Annotation -> List Annotation
  annq-by-kind-step (xs) (kind-name) (i) (len) (acc) (a) =
    if annotation-kind-name (a.kind) == kind-name
      then annq-by-kind-loop xs kind-name (i + 1) len (list-push acc a)
      else annq-by-kind-loop xs kind-name (i + 1) len acc

  annq-by-target : List Annotation, Text -> List Annotation
  annq-by-target (xs) (path) =
    annq-by-target-loop xs path 0 (list-length xs) []

  annq-by-target-loop : List Annotation, Text, Integer, Integer, List Annotation -> List Annotation
  annq-by-target-loop (xs) (path) (i) (len) (acc) =
    if i >= len then acc
    else annq-by-target-step xs path i len acc (list-at xs i)

  annq-by-target-step : List Annotation, Text, Integer, Integer, List Annotation, Annotation -> List Annotation
  annq-by-target-step (xs) (path) (i) (len) (acc) (a) =
    if (a.target).path == path
      then annq-by-target-loop xs path (i + 1) len (list-push acc a)
      else annq-by-target-loop xs path (i + 1) len acc

Section: Rendering

 One line per annotation: the target it is anchored to, its kind, and its
 body. The author and the timestamp are deliberately absent. Perforce
 answers both precisely for the sidecar file, and a maintainer reading an
 invariant wants the invariant.

  annq-line : Annotation -> Text
  annq-line (a) =
    (a.target).path & "  [" & annotation-kind-name (a.kind) & "] " & (a.body)

  annq-render : List Annotation -> Text
  annq-render (xs) = annq-render-loop xs 0 (list-length xs) ""

  annq-render-loop : List Annotation, Integer, Integer, Text -> Text
  annq-render-loop (xs) (i) (len) (acc) =
    if i >= len then acc
    else annq-render-loop xs (i + 1) len (acc & annq-line (list-at xs i) & "\n")

Section: Counting

  annq-count : List Annotation -> Integer
  annq-count (xs) = list-length xs

  annq-count-of-kind : List Annotation, Text -> Integer
  annq-count-of-kind (xs) (kind-name) = list-length (annq-by-kind xs kind-name)

